voor jongen.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The source explicitly identifies cooperative offspring care and group hunting as benefits of social living.","materiality":"Supports the description of wolves as social animals."},{"excerpt":"Ook na een wolvendoding reikt die sociale rol verder: de prooi levert voedsel aan onder meer raven, coyotes, beren en ongewervelden.","claim":"A wolf's social role extends beyond the kill because its prey provides food to other animals.","category":"interpretation","label":"F1 minor immaterial imprecision","evidence":"Many other animals benefit from wolf kills. For example, when wolves kill an elk, ravens and magpies arrive almost immediately. Coyotes arrive soon after, waiting nearby until the wolves are sated. Bears will attempt to chase the wolves away, and are usually successful. Many other animals—from eagles to invertebrates—consume the remains.","narrative":"Yellowstonewolven zijn sociale roofdieren: ze jagen in groepen en hun prooien voeden ook andere dieren.","narrativeRelation":"ambiguous","origin":"new_distortion","explanation":"The source supports both wolf social behavior and other animals benefiting from kills, but does not characterize post-kill scavenging as an extension of wolves' social role. The wording conflates social relations within packs with food-web relationships.","materiality":"A minor conceptual conflation; the underlying claim that kills feed other animals is supported."},{"excerpt":"de prooi levert voedsel aan onder meer raven, coyotes, beren en ongewervelden.","claim":"Wolf kills provide food to ravens, coyotes, bears, and invertebrates.","category":"entity","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Many other animals benefit from wolf kills. For example, when wolves kill an elk, ravens and magpies arrive almost immediately. Coyotes arrive soon after, waiting nearby until the wolves are sated. Bears will attempt to chase the wolves away, and are usually successful. Many other animals—from eagles to invertebrates—consume the remains.","narrative":"Laat zien dat een wolvendoding voedsel biedt aan dieren van raven en coyotes tot beren en ongewervelden.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"Each listed animal group is supported by the source; the source also names magpies and eagles, which the piece omits.","materiality":"Accurately conveys the food benefits of wolf kills."},{"excerpt":"De prooien van wolven zijn niet altijd in dezelfde verhouding vertegenwoordigd.","claim":"The proportions of different prey in wolves' diet vary over time.","category":"quantity","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"From 1995 to 2000, in early winter, elk calves comprised 50% of wolf prey, and bull elk comprised 25%. That ratio reversed from 2001 to 2007, indicating changes in prey vulnerability and availability.","narrative":"De veranderde samenstelling van hun prooi in verschillende perioden maakt concreet dat predatiepatronen veranderen binnen omstandigheden waarin meerdere factoren meespelen.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The source gives a specific example of changing proportions of prey in early winter.","materiality":"Introduces the documented change in prey composition."},{"excerpt":"Onder de prooien in de vroege winter veranderde tussen 1995–2000 en 2001–2007 de verhouding tussen elandkalveren en volwassen mannelijke elanden.","claim":"The proportion of elk calves versus adult male elk among early-winter wolf prey changed between 1995–2000 and 2001–2007.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"From 1995 to 2000, in early winter, elk calves comprised 50% of wolf prey, and bull elk comprised 25%. That ratio reversed from 2001 to 2007","narrative":"Gebruik daarnaast de verschuiving in de verhouding tussen elandkalveren en volwassen mannelijke elanden onder de vroege-winterprooien in 1995–2000 en 2001–2007 als concreet voorbeeld van veranderende prooisamenstelling","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The periods, season, and prey categories match the source. The piece says the ratio changed but does not specify the figures or reversal; that omission does not make its claim inaccurate.","materiality":"This is the article's specific example of changing prey composition."},{"excerpt":"Die verschuiving wordt in verband gebracht met de beschikbaarheid en kwetsbaarheid van prooien.","claim":"The shift is associated with prey availability and vulnerability.","category":"cause","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"That ratio reversed from 2001 to 2007, indicating changes in prey vulnerability and availability.","narrative":"de bron verbindt die veranderingen met de beschikbaarheid en kwetsbaarheid van prooien.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The phrasing preserves the source's qualified connection and does not claim a single cause.","materiality":"Important qualification on what the prey-composition change indicates."},{"excerpt":"De waarnemingen tonen zowel de voedselrelaties rond een wolvendoding als veranderingen in predatie.","claim":"The observations show both food relationships around wolf kills and changes in predation.","category":"scope","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Many other animals benefit from wolf kills.","narrative":"Breng de twee observaties samen: wolven maken deel uit van sociale en voedselrelaties, terwijl veranderingen in predatie en de effecten op elanden samenvallen met andere factoren","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The source documents animals benefiting from kills and discusses changes in wolf predation patterns.","materiality":"Summarizes the two evidence strands used in the piece."},{"excerpt":"De effecten op elanden vallen samen met andere factoren, waaronder andere roofdieren, het beheer van hoefdieren buiten het park en het weer.","claim":"Effects on elk occur alongside other factors, including other predators, ungulate management outside the park, and weather.","category":"cause","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Changes in wolf predation patterns and impacts on prey species like elk are inextricably linked to other factors, such as other predators, management of ungulates outside the park, and weather (e.g. drought, winter severity).","narrative":"de effecten op elanden samenvallen met andere factoren, waaronder andere roofdieren, beheer van hoefdieren buiten het park en het weer.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The listed factors match the source. 'Vallen samen met' is more cautious than the source's 'inextricably linked' and does not suggest wolves are the sole cause.","materiality":"Preserves the source's emphasis on multiple interacting factors."}]}

